Z||000000||Linx||10-16-1999||04:36 PM||||On my '86 SE V-6.  I've already replaced the distributor shaft seal, but Ive still got oil collecting around the base and in that depression in the block (just forward) of the distributor.  Im beginning to suspect that oil is coming up thru the distributor hold-down bolt hole.<P>Anyone seen this?  Im thinking I can coat the bolt with thread locker or somethin'.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||10-16-1999||05:09 PM||||My Formula has this exact same problem.  When I got it, I pulled the distributor, replaced the seal, etc. Put it back in, and it still leakes oil from somewhere in that area.  Not enough that it requires adding any, but just enough to annoy me when I want my engine clean.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||10-16-1999||09:06 PM||||Sometimes oil will leak between the block and intake manifold which is ONLY sealed with RTV. You'd have to remove the manifold and reapply RTV after cleaning the surfaces. ||||reg||1
